WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.120
- My friends, if you do not spend 2018

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.400
completely and obsessively
around Facebook and Instagram,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.531
you will lose.

00:00:08.531 --> 00:00:10.948
(soft music)

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.640
Toys "R" Us did two things
over the last couple decades

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.473
that make no sense.

00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:22.530
One, very early in the 2000's

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.490
they outsourced themselves to Amazon.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.280
They didn't believe in the internet,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.930
17 years ago said let
Amazon do their fulfillment.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.913
Which started people
getting used to buying toys

00:00:30.913 --> 00:00:33.030
on the internet through an Amazon world.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.820
But most importantly,
they just didn't innovate.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.430
And when you don't innovate, you die.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.830
Like when you don't change you die.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.030
The world passes you by.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.050
It's the best example right now

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.090
of how in trouble everybody is

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.283
if they fuckin' rest on their laurels.

00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:52.800
If Toys "R" Us, the
dominant niche retail leader

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.800
of a humongous multi-billion
dollar category, is finished,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.803
what do you think is gonna
happen over the next six years?

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.760
This is a calm before
the social media storm.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.256
This is 2000 all over again.

00:01:06.256 --> 00:01:09.140
The internet came out,
it had a lot of hype,

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.770
the market crashed,
people didn't see returns

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.900
and people left it.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.240
Borders didn't believe in it,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.610
they gave Amazon the infrastructure,

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:16.550
they're out of business.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.880
Blockbuster didn't believe in it,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.360
they let Netflix come in and
put them out of business.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.308
Social media has had a lot
of hype the last two years,

00:01:22.308 --> 00:01:24.310
the next three are gonna be soft

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.440
because people are not
gonna figure out the ROI

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.160
and then people are gonna
be put out of business

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.230
and huge businesses are gonna blow up

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:33.050
and explode and take over in 2013, 14, 15.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:33.883
- Wow.

00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:35.610
- Yeah, that's what's happenin'.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.680
We have a room of
professionals in this room

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.320
who say, well my customers
not on Facebook or Instagram,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.890
maybe they're on LinkedIn.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.910
That is the exact same rationale

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.680
that Netflix put Blockbuster
out of business with.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.550
Blockbuster sat in a room and they said,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.850
our data shows that people
like going to our stores.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.610
By the way, are you really ready to laugh?

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.750
Here's what the report actually said,

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.710
they like the experience
of going to our stores

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.530
because they like the
ability to open and close

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.200
and read the back of the DVD cases.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.070
It gets better, they enjoy the serendipity

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.323
of possibly running into their neighbor.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.350
This is what the report, by the way,

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.310
that's my favorite part
about reports and data,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.150
when you have an agenda

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.750
you can make a report
do a anything you want.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.170
Thank you.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.250
And then finally, they
really like picking up

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.400
popcorn on the way out.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.673
I don't know about you guys,

00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:35.810
